to correct this mistake.

00:15:32.906 --> 00:15:35.060
So, this is what
Microsoft researchers

00:15:35.061 --> 00:15:36.970
and I've highlighted some of

00:15:36.971 --> 00:15:38.880
the important things
and that's where

00:15:38.881 --> 00:15:41.445
the myths I want to clarify is.

00:15:41.446 --> 00:15:44.620
We are growing, and
this is we're growing,

00:15:44.621 --> 00:15:47.350
we're hiring in all areas of

00:15:47.351 --> 00:15:49.730
core computer science and we're

00:15:49.731 --> 00:15:52.330
growing not only
in in the people,

00:15:52.331 --> 00:15:55.920
in research and in our exposure
and our engagement.

00:15:55.921 --> 00:15:57.680
So, with what Sandy was

00:15:57.681 --> 00:16:00.625
mentioning how we engage
with you are we're growing,

00:16:00.626 --> 00:16:02.820
but we're also growing
in our spread.

00:16:02.821 --> 00:16:05.360
So, our recent member of

00:16:05.361 --> 00:16:08.410
the family is
the Montreal, a lab,

00:16:08.411 --> 00:16:10.650
so we're also opening new labs

00:16:10.651 --> 00:16:14.050
and I think this is
important and I would

00:16:14.051 --> 00:16:18.370
love you to share
this and internalize

00:16:18.371 --> 00:16:20.200
this and share this in

00:16:20.201 --> 00:16:23.335
your communities and
with your students.

00:16:23.336 --> 00:16:25.765
Of course, we are
very interested in

00:16:25.766 --> 00:16:29.300
your students as
part of this growth.

