but I'll today,

00:19:44.001 --> 00:19:45.420
just for the
introduction I'll give

00:19:45.421 --> 00:19:48.380
some examples of
historic surprises.

00:19:48.381 --> 00:19:51.160
So one surprise is the Kinect

00:19:51.161 --> 00:19:53.870
which hopefully all of
you have heard about

00:19:53.871 --> 00:19:55.640
which got it's origin from

00:19:55.641 --> 00:19:58.140
Microsoft Research and it's

00:19:58.141 --> 00:19:59.720
a wonderful piece of technology.

00:19:59.721 --> 00:20:04.145
And I think it has
made many children,

00:20:04.146 --> 00:20:07.180
definitely my children-
among the four children,

00:20:07.181 --> 00:20:08.540
I have three daughters
and they love

00:20:08.541 --> 00:20:11.630
the dancing games that
only works with Kinect.

00:20:11.631 --> 00:20:14.560
Whoops, can we go back please?

00:20:14.561 --> 00:20:17.300
Yeah, sorry. Yeah
there because I have

00:20:17.301 --> 00:20:20.290
this red button which I'm
not allowed to press.

00:20:20.291 --> 00:20:21.790
It's always dangerous to get

00:20:21.791 --> 00:20:24.165
something with
a red button in your hand.

00:20:24.166 --> 00:20:29.480
But anyway. But now I'm not
pressing it. Okay, anyway.

00:20:29.481 --> 00:20:31.440
So that's the Kinect,

00:20:31.441 --> 00:20:32.840
that's one of the surprises.

00:20:32.841 --> 00:20:36.140
Another one is actually one
where Eric was involved

00:20:36.141 --> 00:20:40.985
in is from 1998 which we would
call the first smartphone.

00:20:40.986 --> 00:20:45.360
This is another surprise
and, of course,

00:20:45.361 --> 00:20:49.310
we are very proud of
being the source of

00:20:49.311 --> 00:20:54.265
that and it took 10 years
plus to make it really work.

00:20:54.266 --> 00:20:57.010
So this is where
I want to get at.

00:20:57.011 --> 00:21:01.450
So, all our dreams
have come true,

00:21:01.451 --> 00:21:03.810
that is correct, but that doesn't

00:21:03.811 --> 00:21:06.615
mean that we don't
have to work anymore.

00:21:06.616 --> 00:21:11.240
This is a chart we often
think about, well,

00:21:11.241 --> 00:21:13.330
we want to change
the world and we

00:21:13.331 --> 00:21:15.450
want to innovate
and we often hear

00:21:15.451 --> 00:21:20.050
this formula that innovation
is invention times impact.

00:21:20.051 --> 00:21:23.050
And there is a big mountain of

00:21:23.051 --> 00:21:26.675
innovation is what we as
researchers do all the time.

00:21:26.676 --> 00:21:29.300
We do the science,

00:21:29.301 --> 00:21:33.360
and we create new ideas,
and we invent.

00:21:33.361 --> 00:21:36.525
Then there's another mountain

00:21:36.526 --> 00:21:39.865
which is creating impact
out of these ideas,

00:21:39.866 --> 00:21:41.975
pre-creating products and so on.

00:21:41.976 --> 00:21:45.285
These mountains, if you look
at it at the timescale,

00:21:45.286 --> 00:21:47.080
somehow you have to have an idea

00:21:47.081 --> 00:21:49.840
before you at some point
get to the product,

00:21:49.841 --> 00:21:53.555
but there's a big deep
valley between that.

00:21:53.556 --> 00:21:55.590
In the case of the smartphone,

00:21:55.591 --> 00:21:57.600
this valley was 10 years.

00:21:57.601 --> 00:22:00.680
It took 10 years from

00:22:00.681 --> 00:22:04.580
the first prototype of
a smartphone out of the lab of

00:22:04.581 --> 00:22:07.870
Microsoft Research
until nine years until

00:22:07.871 --> 00:22:12.500
Apple really got smartphones out.

00:22:12.501 --> 00:22:14.320
Part of what we do at

00:22:14.321 --> 00:22:18.360
Microsoft Research is
to create this stretch,

00:22:18.361 --> 00:22:20.670
because we've realized
that we can no longer

00:22:20.671 --> 00:22:26.550
just hope that somehow
our ideas will be picked up.

00:22:26.551 --> 00:22:28.820
So that is why we work very

00:22:28.821 --> 00:22:30.680
closely with the product groups

00:22:30.681 --> 00:22:32.320
and I'm going to talk about that.

00:22:32.321 --> 00:22:34.275
In some sense for you,

00:22:34.276 --> 00:22:36.375
this is a great opportunity

00:22:36.376 --> 00:22:42.050
because you're on
the invention side and you also-

00:22:42.051 --> 00:22:44.150
many of you have start-ups

00:22:44.151 --> 00:22:46.370
